  "image_tag": "bench-toolz",
  "instruction": "## Goal\n\nAdd a `peek` function to `toolz.itertoolz` that returns the first element of a sequence together with an equivalent iterable that still contains that first element.\n\n## Observable behavior\n\n```python\nfrom toolz.itertoolz import peek\n\ndef test_peek():\n    assert peek([1, 2, 3, 4]) == (1, (1, 2, 3, 4))\n    assert peek('ABC') == ('A', 'ABC')\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- The new function must be added to `toolz/itertoolz.py` and exposed through `toolz/__init__.py`.\n- Files in scope: `toolz/__init__.py`, `toolz/itertoolz.py`, `toolz/recipes.py`, `toolz/sandbox/core.py`, `toolz/sandbox/parallel.py`, `toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py`.\n- Do not modify existing public API signatures or break existing tests.\n\n## How success is measured\n\nRun the verifier test with:\n\n```\npython -m pytest -q toolz/tests/test_itertoolz.py::test_peek\n```",
